        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Noss, Keith Park\n- Roles: gunner, Air Chief Marshal, soldier, flying ace, Royal Air Force commander\n- Organizations: Royal Air Force\n- Concepts: Military Cross, flying accident, First World War, Second World War\n\nFacts:\n- Keith Park was born on 15 June 1892 and died on 6 February 1975.\n- Keith Park was a New Zealand soldier, a First World War flying ace, and a Second World War Royal Air Force commander.\n- Arthur Noss won a Military Cross while serving as Keith Park's gunner.\n- Arthur Noss was killed in a flying accident shortly after winning the Military Cross.",
